WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.988
A flip makes money once, when it sells, and every month you hold it costs you.

2
00:00:04.988 --> 00:00:09.566
Here's how to check a fix and flip in EquityFoundry before you make an offer.

3
00:00:10.366 --> 00:00:12.425
Choose fix and flip at the top.

4
00:00:12.425 --> 00:00:14.483
It's part of EquityFoundry Pro.

5
00:00:15.283 --> 00:00:19.315
Enter the purchase price, your rehab budget, and the closing costs.

6
00:00:21.813 --> 00:00:23.648
Next, the after-repair value:

7
00:00:23.648 --> 00:00:26.369
what it should sell for once it's finished.

8
00:00:26.369 --> 00:00:29.469
Base it on recent sales of fixed-up homes nearby.

9
00:00:29.469 --> 00:00:34.720
Add how many months until it sells, and your selling costs, like agent commissions.

10
00:00:35.520 --> 00:00:40.830
Then the loan, plus the taxes, insurance and utilities you pay while you own it.

11
00:00:40.830 --> 00:00:43.883
Those holding costs add up, month after month.

12
00:00:44.683 --> 00:00:45.984
Here's your answer.

13
00:00:45.984 --> 00:00:48.314
Projected profit after every cost.

14
00:00:48.314 --> 00:00:55.507
ROI on the cash you put in, and annualized ROI, so you can compare a six month flip with a year long one.

15
00:00:55.507 --> 00:00:59.892
The seventy percent rule shows the most many flippers would pay:

16
00:00:59.892 --> 00:01:03.797
seventy percent of the after-repair value, minus repairs.

17
00:01:04.597 --> 00:01:06.663
This price sits above that line.

18
00:01:06.663 --> 00:01:09.761
Bring the offer down and watch the profit climb.

19
00:01:09.761 --> 00:01:12.213
That's the number to negotiate toward.

20
00:01:13.013 --> 00:01:17.387
The flip breakdown shows every dollar in and out, from purchase to sale.

21
00:01:18.187 --> 00:01:21.344
Save it and compare it with your other deals.

22
00:01:21.344 --> 00:01:25.835
Run your first deal at octopisceslabs dot com slash rental calc.

23
00:01:25.835 --> 00:01:27.168
Forge better deals.
